<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Socialist Party of Chile</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1933">1933</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Socialist Party of Chile is a left-wing political party founded on 19 April 1933 by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marmaduke-grove">Marmaduke Grove</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eugenio-matte">Eugenio Matte</a>, Oscar Schnake, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/salvador-allende">Salvador Allende</a> and other veterans of the short-lived Socialist Republic of 1932. Allende was elected president in 1970 at the head of the Popular Unity coalition. Banned under the dictatorship of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/augusto-pinochet">Augusto Pinochet</a>, the party returned as a leading force of the centre-left after 1990.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/socialist-party-of-chile.jpg" alt="Socialist Party of Chile" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: B1mbo · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Emblem_of_the_Socialist_Party_of_Chile.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
